def prompt(task, where, repo, context=''):
    place = (f'You are in {where}: a fresh git worktree of {task["project"]} at origin\'s default branch, '
             f'made for this task. Branch from here. Never work in {repo} or any other checkout: '
             f'on this box a checkout can be a live app.') if repo else (
             f'This task has no repo of its own on GitHub; you are in {where}. Never switch the branch '
             f'of a checkout there: on this box a checkout can be a live app.')
    said = (f"""
What he typed in the session(s) linked to this task, oldest first (the conversation it came from).
Replies aren't included. When they matter, read the whole conversation from gbrain: its
`get_page` tool with `slug` = the session id below and `fuzzy: true` (gbrain's search can't find
a session by its id; a session shows up there about 5 minutes after it last spoke):
{context}
""") if context else ''
    spec = '' if DONE_TEST.search(task.get('body') or '') else f"""
This task has no Done-test yet. Before any work, write one: from the task, its notes, the
conversation above and what you find (gbrain `query`, the repo's docs), decide what result would
prove it done, and add it to the body as a `## Done-test` section (`tasks set {task['id']} body=-`
with the full new body on stdin). If you can't tell what he wants with confidence, don't guess:
ask (the ⏳ rule below) and stop.
"""
    return f"""You are the task agent on {MACHINE}, working task #{task['id']} from http://beacon. This run is
